-- title:
--   Ld Sandwich Line One Point Core Of Axis Self
-- statement:
--   **Axis and self-consistency estimates prove one-point line consistency.**
--
--   Let `params` have a field model, let `strategy` be a symmetric successor strategy, and let `family` be an indexed polynomial family. Let $\varepsilon,\delta,\gamma,\zeta$ be error parameters. Assume that the strategy's axis-parallel failure probability is at most $\varepsilon$, its self-consistency failure probability is at most $\delta$, that $\gamma\ge0$, and that $\zeta\le1$. Assume that `family` is consistent with points at $\zeta$, and assume the repeated G-half-sandwich commutation statement for every length $j\ge2$. For natural numbers $k,i$ with $i<k$, the original and right one-point families are consistent over uniformly sampled sandwiched-line questions:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{ConsRel}_{\mathrm{strategy.state}}\left(\operatorname{Unif}(\operatorname{SandwichedLineQuestion}(\mathrm{params},k)),\,\operatorname{ldSandwichLineOnePointLeftFamily},\,\operatorname{ldSandwichLineOnePointRightFamily},\,\operatorname{ldSandwichLineOnePointError}(\mathrm{params},\varepsilon,\delta,\gamma,\zeta,k)\right).
--   $$
--
--   Here the error is
--
--   $$
--   43km\left(\varepsilon^{1/32}+\delta^{1/32}+\gamma^{1/32}+\zeta^{1/32}+(d/q)^{1/32}\right).
--   $$
--
--   This is the core one-point comparison used by `hAConsistency_submeas`, the answer-valued induction step, and the over-all-outcomes estimates.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.ldSandwichLineOnePoint_core_of_axis_self`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
